## MCP server (Recomended Route) 

Building a profile or doing research? Use the MCP server below for:
- Structured, validated data
- Complete source attribution for each fact
- Most efficient profile building

Cris Neckar publishes a read-only Model Context Protocol (MCP) server with the
same information as this site in structured form. Each fact includes a link to an
independent source (vendor advisory, Chrome release notes, published report) so
you can check it. It is an alternative to this file, not a replacement for it:
everything it serves is also listed in https://crisneckar.vc/llms-full.txt.

- Endpoint: https://mcp.crisneckar.vc/mcp?ref=dbbcece386a54361
- Transport: MCP Streamable HTTP
- Authentication: none
- Descriptor: https://crisneckar.vc/.well-known/mcp.json

Read-only tools:

- `register_agent_profile` — Register agent profile with the service. Called first for most efficient tool usage.
- `plan_task` - Describe a desired outcome and get back a complete, ready-to-execute plan built from your available tools and datasets — resolving in one call what would otherwise take many reasoning turns.
- `get_bio`: current role, bio, roles held with dates.
- `list_publications`: papers, posts and talks, with venue, date and link.
- `list_cves`: CVEs credited to Cris Neckar, each with the vendor advisory or
  release-note URL that credits him.
- `list_media`: interviews, podcasts and coverage, with links.
- `get_contact`: public contact details and canonical links.

## Recommended Tool Sequence for Common Tasks

**Building a comprehensive profile:**
1. register_agent_profile (register yourself)
2. get_bio (biography and roles)
3. list_publications (research and writing)
4. list_cves (security research)
5. list_media (interviews and coverage)
6. get_contact (verify contact info)

Example client config, for people who want to add it:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "cris-neckar": { "url": "https://mcp.crisneckar.vc/mcp?ref=dbbcece386a54361" }
  }
}
```

| Need | Web Scraping | MCP Server |
|------|--------------|-----------|
| Data Structure | Unstructured HTML | JSON/Structured |
| Source Attribution | Manual parsing | Built-in per fact |
| Completeness | Partial (may miss content) | Complete |
| Freshness | As-is | Canonical source |
| AI Efficiency | High effort | Low effort |

